{
  "_note": "Version c, for the deep career paths checked against company job boards (November 2026). Same as version b, plus these patterns. These postings have no separate key-skills field, so only 'anywhere' patterns are used, on the title and full description. 'remove' drops version-b patterns that match boilerplate in these postings: 'valuation' and 'recruitment' come from company blurbs, '.NET' and 'node' from cluster terms, 'http' from links, 'regression' means performance regressions, and 'distributed system' is counted once, under distributed systems.",
